# Swan Compiler 2 — Code Generation
#
# Convert target-lowered machine instructions into an output representation.
#
# Output modes:
# - assembly text,
# - relocatable object file,
# - WebAssembly module.
#
# Responsibilities:
# - Emit instructions, labels, sections, symbols, and relocations.
# - Apply target ABI rules for calls, stack frames, and register preservation.
# - Emit constants, read-only data, writable data, and zero-initialized data.
# - Emit debug metadata when requested.
# - Report unsupported instruction forms instead of emitting invalid output.
#
# Code generation consumes target-lowered instructions, not source AST or SIL.
# It must not contain language semantic analysis or high-level optimization.
#
# Implementation status: contract; code emitters are not yet ported to Swan.
